          'The blank page is a problem of too many options rather than too few ideas, and the reliable remedy is constraint. Give yourself three pitches, a fixed rhythmic cell, a single dynamic, or a duration of forty seconds, and the question changes from what should I write to what can I do with this. Almost every composer works this way in practice, and much of the repertoire you admire was produced under constraints imposed by a commission, an ensemble, an occasion or a self-set rule. Constraint is not a limitation on creativity; it is the condition under which creativity operates.',
